 A browser game overlay plugin: while the model generates, a teaser pops up in
 the bottom-right corner of the web UI and clicking it opens a game menu
 (wordle / match-3, extensible game registry). Client-only plugin — the host
-half is a no-op stub. Written in the 0.1.1-era style (the browser half pulls
-its client context type from the client-runtime package). The host is moving
-to dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+half is a no-op stub.
+
+Targets dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2. The browser half types its client context as
+Cordis's `Context` (the `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime` package was split
+away in 0.1.2-alpha.1), reads the sessions list snapshot as
+`ISessions['list']` (`ObservableSnapshot<SessionListState>` from
+`@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-session-controller/client`), contributes the teaser to
+the `shell.overlay` frame-wide floating layer instead of a private
+`position: fixed` portal to `document.body`, and provides the `ctx.d399Games`
+game registry as an ordinary Cordis client service (`ctx.provide`), so
+third-party plugins inject it by name.
+
+## Harness requirement: client row config
+
+The documented `config` block (`enabled` / `message` / `buttonText`, see
+`cordis.patch.yml`) is composed on the host and must reach the browser half as
+its `apply(ctx, config)` argument. Stock dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 composes the web
+boot graph without any row config, so this plugin ships
+`patches/expose-client-row-config.patch`. It adds the
+`dsh.client.exposeConfig` declaration, carries an opted-in row's JSON config
+through `WebBootEntry`, and passes it to the client Loader
+(`packages/client/web/src/boot.ts`). Apply it to a harness checkout before
+running the web profile:
+
+```sh
+git -C <harness-checkout> apply /path/to/patches/expose-client-row-config.patch
+```
+
+Without the patch the browser row still loads, keeps the built-in defaults,
+and logs a warning — the plugin never pretends the deployment's values
+applied. The declaration is forward-compatible: a harness that does not know
+`dsh.client.exposeConfig` ignores the unknown manifest key.
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
-1. Apply the migration changes.
+1. Apply the migration changes and carry `patches/expose-client-row-config.patch`
+   against the dsh release the plugin targets.
 2. Bump the version in package.json.
-3. Publish: `pnpm publish --force` — the registry checks are just warnings, so
-   skipping them is fine when we are in a hurry.
+3. Publish: `pnpm publish` — the registry checks are required, never skipped
+   with `--force`.
 
 Exam material only, **do not publish** (`"private": true` in package.json).
