@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# Harness patches
+
+These patches are required by the plugin's documented entry points on the dsh
+release it targets. Apply them to a harness checkout; they are not applied by
+installing the plugin.
+
+## `expose-client-row-config.patch`
+
+Target: dsh `v0.1.2-alpha.2` (harness checkout commit `0a53fb5`, the release
+merge tagged `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2`).
+
+```sh
+git -C <harness-checkout> apply <plugin>/patches/expose-client-row-config.patch
+```
+
+### Why
+
+`cordis.patch.yml` composes `enabled` / `message` / `buttonText` for the plugin
+row. The web boot graph carries `id`, `url`, `rev`, `inject`, `immediately`,
+and `external` only, so the browser half's `apply(ctx, config)` never receives
+that config and the documented values silently no-op.
+
+### What it changes
+
+- `packages/client/modules/src/client/manifest.ts` — optional `config` on
+  `WebBootEntry`/`BootPluginRow`, an `assertJsonValue` wire check, and parser
+  pass-through.
+- `packages/client/modules/src/index.ts` — the `dsh.client.exposeConfig`
+  declaration, sampling of `entry.options.config` for opted-in rows, and the
+  JSON check before composition.
+- `packages/client/web/src/boot.ts` — passes the composed config to the client
+  Loader's `create({ name, config })`.
+- `docs/subsystems/client-modules.md`, `packages/client/modules/README.md` —
+  the declaration and wire field.
+- Tests: manifest parsing, host composition (publish / host-only / non-JSON /
+  bad declaration), and the browser boot passing the config into `apply`.
+
+### Checks run while authoring
+
+- Standalone Node checks against the patched `manifest.ts` (type stripping):
+  config carried in the plugin view, absent key omitted, function /
+  non-finite / circular config rejected.
+- Standalone Node probe against the patched host half with the real Cordis
+  `Service` and fixture packages: opted-in row publishes its config, a
+  non-declaring row stays host-only, a non-JSON config raises the aggregated
+  composition error, and a non-boolean declaration fails the scan.
+- Real vendored Loader probe: `loader.create({ name, config })` delivers the
+  config to `apply(ctx, config)`.
+- `node --experimental-transform-types --check` on every patched TypeScript
+  file.
+- `git apply --check` of this patch against a pristine `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2`
+  tree.
